      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "To the north, Gila Crossing borders Komatke and St. Johns, while Santa Cruz lies just across the Gila River in Pinal County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gila_Crossing%2C_Arizona",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Downtown Phoenix is only 16 miles northeast of Gila Crossing, making the community a short drive from the city’s core.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gila_Crossing%2C_Arizona",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Gila River Transit links Gila Crossing with nearby Komatke and Maricopa Colony, providing a vital regional connection.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gila_Crossing%2C_Arizona",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The K‑8 Gila Crossing Community School, a tribal institution tied to the Bureau of Indian Education, is located in neighboring Komatke.",
